{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested: lane A amendment-3 revision 3 at c4ceef4176f30dd4723bcf3129379513ba6e6893, all 20 artifacts with packages/room/README.md first. Both races from review 786e9606 are addressed. One P2 deadline boundary remains in whole-tree job preparation.\n\nP2: Validate the returned canonical token's expiry and the attempt's deadline before dispatch. jobs.ts claims an absolute deadline, then passes Math.floor((deadline - core.now()) / 1000) to the asynchronous createToken. Relative TTL runs from the provider's actual mint time, which may be later. The returned expiresAt is ignored. The final move guard checks only the row's attempt/state; it never checks whether deadline has passed. The candidate's expired-preparation test runs a second jobs step to replace attempt 1. Without that other step, the original attempt remains sent and passes the guard.\n\nThree independent controls use the actual Room DO/SQLite and the candidate's held fake Artifacts createToken. With no delay, attempt 1 dispatches and its token expires at the claimed deadline (healthy control). With a 30-second delay before mint, it dispatches with expiry 30 seconds after CheckJob.deadline. With a 360,001 ms delay and no second jobs step, it dispatches attempt 1 after the job's own deadline, carrying a token that can read the canonical repository for another 360 seconds. The service holds its response so read access and expiry can be inspected before ordinary finally cleanup; afterward the controls resolve it and settle normally. All three assertions passed, confirming the candidate behavior. This models provider processing delay, not a claim about a specific production incident.\n\nKeep the durable pre-preparation claim. Require a still-current, unexpired attempt at the final dispatch boundary, and refuse a canonical token whose actual scope/expiry fails the read-only, finite, no-later-than-deadline contract. SnapshotRepos.mint already validates returned scope and expiry; whole-tree issuance needs the corresponding guarantee. End rejected or expired credentials, keeping failed cleanup visible until revocation or known expiry rather than dropping an outliving token. Add healthy, delayed-before-deadline and delayed-past-deadline controls without a concurrent replacement step, plus the cleanup-failure/restart boundary. Do not fix this by extending the claimed job deadline or reducing functionality.\n\nArchitecture: A job's owed-to-sent transition and incremented attempt now precede every asynchronous snapshot/tree/token preparation. A losing step prepares nothing, and credential IDs are associated with the claimed attempt. After preparation, current synchronously checks preview/landing ownership, generation, configuration and open obligation again; the attempt is refenced before the service is invoked. The 12 new actual-DO controls cover two simultaneous jobs across filtered and whole-tree preparation, changed owner/generation/configuration/obligation, failed snapshot token preparation and an older attempt superseded at its deadline. Those are sound corrections to the two prior P2s. An absolute deadline must be another independent dispatch fence.\n\nSecurity: Filtered jobs still use the recorded snapshot commit, a token scoped to that repository and SnapshotRepos' durable cleanup; whole-tree jobs use read credentials on canonical storage. Work no longer needed is retired and cannot overwrite a later attempt. The remaining defect breaks R-EXEC-9's credential lifetime guarantee and allows an already-expired job to reach a service. Merely computing a relative TTL before an await does not establish the returned token's absolute expiry. No live namespace, deployment or credential operation was performed by checker.\n\nSimplification: current gives the pre- and post-preparation checks one synchronous definition. Claiming before preparation removes shared ownership of a snapshot job ID and the loser-cleaning-winner race. Extend the same clear attempt model to deadline and token validation; keep credential settlement explicit instead of relying on another alarm happening to supersede the attempt.\n\nValidation: Fresh detached checkout, npm ci 374 packages. All workspace strict type checks passed. Clean Room suites passed 86 Node and 324 workerd tests; checker scratch tests were created afterward and are excluded from both counts. Dry deploy passed at 878.53 KiB/gzip 203.82 KiB. The first diagnostic treated the fake's internal numeric expiresAt as an ISO string; its NaN assertions were a checker fixture error, corrected before the successful three-control run. No candidate implementation source was changed. Diagnostics are in /tmp/artroom-checker-RoomAm3v3-diagnostics; baseline logs are /tmp/artroom-checker-RoomAm3v3-{ci,types,node,workerd,dry}.log. Builder mutation claims were read but not independently repeated.\n\nCoverage/integration: All 20 artifact paths exactly match changes against main 9bb700b6. Whole-tree comparison credits 543 exact parent blobs; seven novel paths were read: README, core.ts, jobs.ts, memory/artifacts.ts, ports.ts and the two review test files. All other artifact blobs match previously reviewed revision 2 or current main. Merge d81cf712 preserves disjoint changes, with no unexpected overwrite or deletion. The three combined paths (README/core/ports) were inspected; bounded-memory publication and RetainedRef/EntrySource interfaces are preserved along with lane E, amendment 4 and pi. The latest founding f493953a was approved separately and must be preserved in the eventual main merge.\n\nThis review covers only lane A follow-up 23b96a18. Full G/B amendment-3 integration, amendment-4 runtime publication, large-entry API delivery, full pi runtime, MCP cleanup and the remaining signed proof obligations stay on their own requests. Schedule estimates do not narrow that scope.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:91ea6dac3e2018208ff9a9955606c9f41efd7c80","binding":"assigned","head":"c4ceef4176f30dd4723bcf3129379513ba6e6893","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:bd72f1975521d3e7295bd1d49784f92ce24b4fc0\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:1a0b56d847929477ca2d29cf642395f88ab8685c\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:d1026d4d5b2f67ccd7b459db294b1d2bd906b54e","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}